  "what_changed": "Upstream kart 0.3.7 and base 0.2.3: the pit can start or end a freeplay game for the whole fleet (GK_CMD_GAME = 9), which a kart Heltec forwards to its Pi. A paired M5 kart has no Pi and joins from its Core2, so its Heltec build answers that command REJECTED and changes nothing, instead of acknowledging a game it did not join. The three Heltec kart images and the base image are rebuilt; Core2 and repeater images are the 2026-11-13-race-screen files, byte for byte.",
  "compatibility": "LoRa protocol: one new command id (9); older karts acknowledge and ignore it, and nothing else changed. Both boards of a kart need the race-screen pair for the grid countdown. Host Heltec, host Pi server, player Heltec and player Core2 must all be from this source for course download, JOIN and FIRE. An M5 kart cannot join a ROAM freeplay and does not act on a pit-started game.",
